# Store and check out every text file with LF line endings on every OS, overriding a
# machine's core.autocrlf setting. Firefox's source uses LF, and our scripts and CI run on
# Linux, so Windows-style CRLF copies only cause trouble.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Patch files must reach the patch tool exactly as exported, byte for byte: never convert
# their line endings. (A few upstream files use CRLF on purpose; their patches must keep it.)
*.patch -text
*.diff -text
